WEBVTT

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:07.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Friday the twenty-seventh. Everyone hearing me? Tom's not in today.</v>

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:12.619
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, got you. Bit of a hum from someone's end.</v>

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:17.989
<v David Whitfield>That's probably mine. Office fan's got a bearing like a bag of spanners.</v>

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.100
<v Priya Raman>It's all right, we can hear over it.</v>

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:30.309
<v Marcus Hale>More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Proper one, not those individually wrapped things.</v>

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:37.939
<v Hannah Price>And the charity bake sale on Friday is today, so we're absolutely surrounded by cake.</v>

00:00:39.429 --> 00:00:42.579
<v Callum Reid>Dangerous place to hold a morning meeting, that office.</v>

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:44.719
<v Marcus Hale>I'm showing considerable restraint, actually.</v>

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:50.679
<v Sarah Okafor>Very proud of you. Right, quick round on where we're at, then today's bits. Jamie?</v>

00:00:51.929 --> 00:01:00.679
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah so, the shift handover report — I've had a first look, nothing major so far. I'm partway through it; it hasn't gone round yet.</v>

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:10.290
<v Sarah Okafor>My function test's stuck. Production won't give us a window, so I can't get on with that.</v>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:15.719
<v Callum Reid>It's wall-to-wall on the plan at the minute. Not much breathing space anywhere.</v>

00:01:17.989 --> 00:01:19.189
<v David Whitfield>Mm. Understood.</v>

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.609
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tom asked me to say his leak inspection's all done. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:26.379 --> 00:01:27.579
<v Hannah Price>Lovely, thanks.</v>

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:37.409
<v Callum Reid>Haley asked me to pass on his pre-use checks while his mic was playing up before we started. They're all done.</v>

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:39.849
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Reidy.</v>

00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:48.409
<v Marcus Hale>And I'm audible now, hopefully — I've got the downtime for the Atlas agreed with production. Booking's sorted.</v>

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:51.290
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, heard every word of that.</v>

00:01:53.629 --> 00:01:59.579
<v Sarah Okafor>One other bit from me: I already swapped the filter on the GT1 compressor yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:01.280
<v David Whitfield>Ah, right. Cheers.</v>

00:02:03.349 --> 00:02:12.099
<v Priya Raman>Just an observation from earlier: I saw the pressure on the barrel on three dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:13.789 --> 00:02:15.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Back where it normally sits?</v>

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:21.530
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, normal reading again. Nobody touched anything. Just mentioning what I saw.</v>

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Right, today's work.</v>

00:02:27.039 --> 00:02:32.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley, can you check the guarding on the Arburg? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.810
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the Arburg straight away.</v>

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.960
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, physical guarding you're talking about?</v>

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, the guarding. Not asking for an electrical test.</v>

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.780
<v Marcus Hale>Got you. That's my first stop.</v>

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:55.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, could you inspect the pop valve for leaks, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:01.449
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll inspect the pop valve for leaks when I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:05.889
<v David Whitfield>Just a leak inspection, nothing being stripped?</v>

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:08.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, just the inspection.</v>

00:03:09.199 --> 00:03:10.400
<v Hannah Price>Fine by me.</v>

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:17.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Reidy, can you write up the near miss at Injection Moulding Line 1 first thing tomorrow?</v>

00:03:18.759 --> 00:03:22.610
<v Callum Reid>Tomorrow as in Saturday, yeah? Just checking I've heard that right.</v>

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:31.189
<v Callum Reid>Right, accepted. I'll write up the near miss at Injection Moulding Line 1 first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:36.250
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, I nearly spoke over you there. Carry on.</v>

00:03:36.889 --> 00:03:43.189
<v David Whitfield>There's also the pressure drop on the line one HPU, Saz. That needs investigating — top priority please.</v>

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:52.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the line one HPU by the end of the week. I'll treat that as top priority.</v>

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Blimey, Friday already. This week's disappeared.</v>

00:03:57.669 --> 00:04:02.919
<v Sarah Okafor>It has, but yes, by the end of the week is what I'm committing to.</v>

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.000
<v David Whitfield>Okay, thanks, Saz.</v>

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.229
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's the main production worry from my side.</v>

00:04:10.689 --> 00:04:16.990
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, did someone say something then? Teams keeps leaving a gap and then giving me everyone at once.</v>

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.100
<v Priya Raman>Only Reidy. You're caught up.</v>

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:22.639
<v Jamie Brennan>Friday morning internet. Even that's had enough.</v>

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we'll leave it there. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.310
<v Hannah Price>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.949
<v Callum Reid>Cheers.</v>

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.290
<v Marcus Hale>See you in a bit.</v>
